## .NET build outputs
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.idea/
*.pdb

## Publish output (generated by `dotnet publish`)
dist/

## OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

## Source backups — convention is `.bak-<reason>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>` (fact #380).
## `*.bak` alone matched NOTHING: every backup file leaked into `git status`
## (verified 2026-10-16 with an empty repo). 24 of them were sitting untracked.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak-*.*
*.gitignore.bak-*

## Local-only debug tooling — hardcodes C:\Users\yaoyx\... and D:\hermes-工作目录\...
## Publishing it to a public repo leaks personal paths.
probe-runner/

## Scratch files from debugging sessions
_tmp_*
_tmp_*.*

## Local-only rule snippets (contain the user's real absolute paths)
instagram_rule_snippet.md

## Test artifacts
TestResults/
coverage/
*.coverage

## Secrets — never commit
*.env
.env.local
secrets.yaml
